Console lines (window mode only; alert = stderr) and the supervisor state each is emitted in (mine):
1. 'unreagent: Agent exited (exit N) — restart N[/M] in D' — agent OnRunEnd with Restart > 0: emitted on the loop right after restarts++ and backoff = time.After(D), so a restart is armed; never for Restart 0 (give-up, used-up maxRestarts, policy), never for a run a waiting stop took (OnRunEnd needs desired; TestStopWinsOverAnExitReadyWithIt), never once ctx is done (TestNoRunEndDuringTheShutdown). Residual: a shutdown that comes after the line, within D, cancels that restart; and a Ctrl-C that kills the foreground agent before the launcher's ctx is done is a run that ended on its own (same race as finishLocked's comment). The log has the same restart line in both cases.
2. 'unreagent: [ue] exited (<exit>)' and, with a restart armed, 'unreagent: [ue] restart N[/M] in D' — the log's two lines, same state rules as 1. 'unreagent: [ue] start held until the last run's crash reporter has finished' — editor OnStartHeld for an Automatic start: emitted where the supervisor sets held (lingerDone != nil), same text by construction (supervisor.HeldLine); this is what keeps line 'restart N in D' true after k154: the log says the same pair.
3. '<agentEnded> agent.onExit=leave — editor/MCP keep running. Ctrl-C stops the launcher.' / '... agent.onExit=shutdown — stopping everything.' (stdout, console.show), e.g. 'Agent crashed. agent.onExit=leave — …', 'Agent exited. agent.onExit=shutdown — …', 'Agent did not start: <err>. agent.onExit=leave — …' — in OnExit, i.e. the agent is not restarted; agentEnded reads LastError as the exit prompt does.
